CPU fallback, resumable matching and Cambridge image path for kocurvik/threeview @
b43383efba129b8d90e2709092dac6dc87cbbea1, for task 1.6 (triplet generation on machines without CUDA:
abl-dell, the laptop). Applied by scripts/build_seed_code.sh after threeview.patch.

- datasets/prepare_im.py and utils/matching.py hard-code .cuda(); use DEVICE = cuda if available, else cpu.
- LightGlue matching ran with autograd on (only extraction is no_grad); run it under torch.inference_mode().
- Matching is resumable: the match file is flushed every 50 triplets and closed at the end, and a rerun with
  the same seed reopens it, keeps the triplets already there and continues (an unreadable file starts over).
  A reboot mid-run otherwise loses hours of matching.
- For Cambridge, get_dataset_paths expects images in <scene>/<scene>/ (hloc layout); the original zips keep
  them in <scene>/, so fall back to that when <scene>/<scene> does not exist. model_train comes from
  scripts/cambridge_nvm_to_colmap.py.

